{% doc %}
  Global ARIA live regions.

  Rendered EXACTLY ONCE per document, from the layout. Never render this inside
  a section, snippet or component: duplicate `aria-live` containers cause screen
  readers to announce the same message two or more times, and the duplicate ids
  make `document.getElementById` non-deterministic.

  Components must not create their own live regions either. They write into
  these two shared ones through the helpers in `assets/utilities.js`:

    import { announce, announceUrgent } from '@theme/utilities';

    announce(Theme.strings.itemAdded);        // polite  -> #LiveRegion
    announceUrgent(Theme.strings.cartError);  // assertive -> #LiveRegionAssertive

  Choosing a region:
    polite    — status that can wait for a pause in speech: cart updated,
                filters applied, results count changed, cart updated.
    assertive — errors and blocking states the customer must hear immediately:
                failed add-to-cart, invalid discount code, form validation.

  Both regions are `aria-atomic="true"`, so the full message is re-read on every
  change rather than only the diff. Both are visually hidden, never `display:
  none` — a hidden-by-display region is ignored by assistive technology.

  @example
    {% render 'live-region' %}
{% enddoc %}

<div
  id="LiveRegion"
  class="visually-hidden"
  role="status"
  aria-live="polite"
  aria-atomic="true"
></div>

<div
  id="LiveRegionAssertive"
  class="visually-hidden"
  role="alert"
  aria-live="assertive"
  aria-atomic="true"
></div>
